merc-area is the format bridge at the heart of the MUD Builder: a pure, dependency-free, isomorphic TypeScript parser and emitter for Merc 2.4 .are area files, written as a line-faithful mirror of merc-mud/2.4/src/db.c (+db2.c) loaders so that anything db.c can boot round-trips losslessly (verified against the entire shipped area corpus in roundtrip.test.ts). It performs no I/O — the server (apps/mud-builder-server) and the browser client (apps/mud-builder-client) both consume it directly. Strings that db.c resolves through lookup tables are stored verbatim; flags are stored numerically (db.c accepts decimal). Legacy #MOBOLD/#OBJOLD sections are rejected with a clear error (unused by the corpus).
